# Dev-mode only. Vite loads this for `vite` (development mode) and never for
# `vite build`, so nothing here reaches a production bundle.
#
# Compiles in src/e2eInit.ts, which lets Playwright open the app already signed
# in via ?e2eToken/?e2eUser. Without it every UI spec lands on the auth screen.
# It lives here rather than in the CI workflow because the token this repo
# pushes with has no `workflow` scope; setting it in .github/workflows/ci.yml
# would be the tidier home if that ever changes.
#
# Not a way in: e2eInit only stores a token the server already signed. You
# cannot forge a session with it, only re-use one you were legitimately issued.
VITE_E2E=1
